===========================================================================
4. INTEGER DIVISION PITFALL: C/VERILOG TRUNCATION VS PYTHON FLOOR
===========================================================================
    x |    x / 4 (C/Verilog) |      x // 4 (Python) |   Match?
-----------------------------------------------------------------
   -7 |                   -1 |                   -2 | NO (MISMATCH)
   -5 |                   -1 |                   -2 | NO (MISMATCH)
   -4 |                   -1 |                   -1 |      YES
   -1 |                    0 |                   -1 | NO (MISMATCH)
    0 |                    0 |                    0 |      YES
    1 |                    0 |                    0 |      YES
    4 |                    1 |                    1 |      YES
    5 |                    1 |                    1 |      YES
    7 |                    1 |                    1 |      YES
-----------------------------------------------------------------
Explanation: In C and Verilog-2001, integer division '/' truncates towards zero.
For negative numbers (e.g. -5 / 4 = -1, but -5 // 4 = -2), truncation and floor differ.
By adding non-negative bias B = L * 2^15, the dividend is ALWAYS strictly non-negative,
completely eliminating any discrepancy between C/Verilog truncation and mathematical floor!
===========================================================================
